as\nAnimas to Cheraw to near Rocky Ford. Movement was southeast at 25\nmph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph and penny size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nLa Junta, North La Junta, Rocky Ford, Las Animas, Swink, Cheraw,\nHasty, John Martin Reservoir, and Fort Lyon.","ends":"2026-08-16T19:00:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Crowley County; La Junta Vicinity/Otero County; Western Kiowa County; Las Animas Vicinity/Bent County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.29159b5117baed708c9ae8b3b4a8672890debd97.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.29159b5117baed708c9ae8b3b4a8672890debd97.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued August 16 at 6:10PM MDT until August 16 at 7:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"SVRPUB\n\nThe National Weather Service in Pueblo has issued a\n\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...\nNortheastern Otero County in southeastern Colorado...\nNorthwestern Prowers County in southeastern Colorado...\nWestern Kiowa County in southeastern Colorado...\nNorthern Bent County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 700 PM MDT.\n\n* At 610 PM MDT, severe thunderstorms were located along a line\nextending from 13 miles northwest of Eads to 6 miles southeast of\nHaswell to near Blue Lake, moving east at 35 mph.\n\nHAZARD...60 mph wind gusts and nickel size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Expect damage to roofs, siding, and trees.\n\n* Locations impacted include...\nEads, Haswell, Neeoshe Reservoir, Sweetwater Reservoir, Blue Lake,\nNeegronda Reservoir, Arlington, Queens Reservoir, and Chivington.","ends":"2026-08-16T19:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Bent, CO; Kiowa, CO; Otero, CO; Prowers, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a84ded0832ebf4bcffc6e9d181b8e165700974b3.001.1","url"